@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
title class diagram - C++ ViveMoveItServer node

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Monospace

class ViveMoveItServer <<rclcpp::Node>> {
  -arm_group_: string = "arm"
  -planning_frame_: string = "base_footprint"
  -end_effector_link_: string = "arm_tool_link"
  -arm_control_rate_hz_: double = 100
  -latest_controller_pose_: CartesianPose
  -controller_anchor_: CartesianPose
  -tool_anchor_: CartesianPose
  -filtered_target_: CartesianPose
  -target_linear_velocity_: Vector3d
  -target_angular_velocity_: Vector3d
  -arm_requested_: bool
  -arm_rearm_required_: bool
  -arm_tracking_: bool
  -onHandActive(message): void
  -onHandTarget(message): void
  -onServoStatus(message): void
  -onRobotDescription(message): void
  -updateArmControl(): void
  -updateMappedTarget(): void
  -lookupToolPose(pose): bool
  -constrainTarget(target, was_clamped): bool
  -publishServoTwist(linear, angular): void
  -publishResolvedRateJointCommand(linear, angular): bool
  -armJacobian(chain_position, jacobian): bool
  -visibilityPostureCost(chain_position): double
  -visibilityAvoidanceVelocity(chain_position, jacobian, safety_scale): VectorXd
  -singularityEscapeVelocity(chain_position, jacobian): VectorXd
  -updateJointLimitRecovery(time): bool
  -rebaseUnreachableTargetIfNeeded(result, tool, time): bool
  -haltArm(timeout, reason): void
  -updateHeadControl(): void
  -onGripperOpening(message): void
  -updateBaseControl(): void
}

class "redundant_ik" as RedundantIK <<C++ library>> {
  +solveRedundantVelocityIk(jacobian, twist, joints, limits, secondary, options): RedundantIkResult
  +minimumSingularValue(jacobian): double
  +normalizedUpwardSlope(start, end): double
  +upwardSegmentPenalty(start, end, activation): double
  +lowElbowPreferenceCost(start, elbow, target, weight): double
  +projectIntoTaskNullspace(jacobian, preference): VectorXd
  +removeOpposingSecondaryComponent(priority, candidate): VectorXd
  +inwardJointLimitRecoveryVelocity(joints, limits, margins): VectorXd
  .. orientation-first task hierarchy ..
  .. J7 -> J6 -> J5 -> J3 -> J2 -> J4 -> J1 activation ..
  .. per-joint saturation + residual fallback ..
  .. singularity escape > compatible centering/visibility ..
  .. per-joint hard/predictive margins ..
}

class "control_math" as ControlMath <<C++ library>> {
  +normalizeQuaternion(q): bool
  +controllerControlPose(pose, offset, alignment): CartesianPose
  +mapControllerDeltaToTool(current, controller_anchor, tool_anchor, scale): CartesianPose
  +orientationError(target, current): Vector3d
  +lowPassPose(previous, target, cutoff, dt): CartesianPose
  +poseFeedback(error, gain, deadband): Vector3d
  +clampVectorNorm(vector, limit): Vector3d
  +rateLimitVector(current, target, rate, dt): Vector3d
  +constrainWorkspacePosition(position, radius, min_z, max_z): bool
}

class RealtimeSetup <<free function>> {
  +configureRealtime(node): RealtimeResult
  .. attempts ..
  mlockall(MCL_CURRENT | MCL_FUTURE)
  pthread_setschedparam(SCHED_FIFO)
  pthread_setaffinity_np(optional)
}

class "tf2_ros::Buffer" as Buffer
class "rclcpp::SingleThreadedExecutor" as Executor
class PoseStamped
class TwistStamped
class JointJog
class JointTrajectory
class Bool
class Float64
class Int8
class JointState

ViveMoveItServer --> ControlMath : all Cartesian math
ViveMoveItServer --> RedundantIK : seven-joint velocity solve
ViveMoveItServer --> Buffer : latest tool TF
RealtimeSetup --> ViveMoveItServer : reads settings / sets status
Executor o-- ViveMoveItServer : timers + latest-value callbacks
PoseStamped --> ViveMoveItServer : head + hand input
Bool --> ViveMoveItServer : arm/base gates
Float64 --> ViveMoveItServer : gripper input
Int8 --> ViveMoveItServer : Servo status
JointState --> ViveMoveItServer : measured fingers
ViveMoveItServer --> TwistStamped : Cartesian action diagnostic
ViveMoveItServer --> JointJog : Servo joint command
ViveMoveItServer --> JointTrajectory : head/gripper commands

note bottom of ViveMoveItServer
  One compiled process owns clutching and the 100 Hz pose loop.
  Actual arm_3->arm_4 and arm_4->arm_5 slopes feed upward penalties;
  arm_3->arm_4 also has a bounded low-elbow target.
  Visibility yields near singularities and protected joint margins.
  Servo joint-bound status triggers inward-only recovery and target rebasing.
  No Python motion node or separate pose bridge is in the arm path.
  Deadman/timeout publishes repeated zero twist/joint commands and requires re-clutch.
end note

@enduml
